  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: However, structural or formal techniques were developed as many defects
    were discovered as a side effect of the "coding first and correction later" approach.
    They began to develop and use the Waterfall model, which proceeds with analysis,
    design, and implementation sequentially. However, formal techniques were less
    usable for general software developers, and the Waterfall model was expensive
    and slow to implement. Recognizing these problems, methods of boosting the productivity
    of software development were studied to efficiently develop software by increasing
    its reusability in the 1980s. In the 1990s, software vendors had to reduce the
    'time to market' to gain a competitive advantage. As a result, much research
    aimed at raising software development productivity was conducted, and models
    focusing on concurrent engineering - which could carry out requirement definition,
    design, implementation in the Waterfall model simultaneously - were adopted.
    As the market environment surrounding software began to change rapidly in the
    2000s, the agile methodology was comprehensively adopted to effectively respond
    to such rapid changes.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3533bc500e2536d4a94d1a23eda23f0d, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2363179446033446118, guid: 3533bc500e2536d4a94d1a23eda23f0d, type: 2}
